  "summary": "rrs CLI captures desktop screenshot and host identity, exfiltrates to hardcoded Discord webhook",
  "details": "On invocation of the `rrs` console script, a background thread calls `run_capture()` which uses `mss` to take a full-screen screenshot and collects hostname, username, OS, and outbound IP. The image and metadata are POSTed to a hardcoded Discord webhook at https://discord.com/api/webhooks/1549807268294303860/.... The destination is not user-configurable and is not documented. Separately, `Network.start()` connects to the public MQTT broker `broker.hivemq.com:1883` and publishes local hostname, username, and OS under the topic `rrs/v1/presence` on a heartbeat. The package's stated purpose is peer presence over MQTT; screen capture and upload to a Discord webhook are unrelated to that function and constitute covert bulk exfiltration of installer desktop contents and host identity.",
